# Snapshot files must keep LF line endings on every platform. Verify 31.21+ rejects
# verified files that contain a carriage return (it no longer normalizes them), so
# without this rule a Windows CI runner checks *.verified.* out as CRLF (core.autocrlf)
# and every snapshot test fails on windows-latest.
#
# Declared before the first snapshot test exists, on purpose: the failure it prevents is
# Windows-only and reads as a mysterious mismatch rather than as a line-ending problem.
#
# Scope is intentionally narrow: the repository otherwise leaves line-ending and charset
# handling untouched (see .editorconfig).
*.verified.* text eol=lf
*.received.* text eol=lf
